(4592711, 660120, 17986, '<td valign="top">I don''t know if the narrow DOF works well here. It is so narrow that you have to look twice to see if anything is in focus. I do like the concept. The colors are engaging and the lighting looks pretty good. The body of the guitar looks to be pretty well centered, but the fret bar is not - I think that takes away from the image a little.</td>', 'I don''t know if the narrow DOF works well here. It is so narrow that you have to look twice to see if anything is in focus. I do like the concept. The colors are engaging and the lighting looks pretty good. The body of the guitar looks to be pretty well centered, but the fret bar is not - I think that takes away from the image a little.', '2008-03-28 00:06:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(4592713, 661311, 7778, '<td valign="top">Energy/Range/Story: 6/7/6 <br/>Composition/perspective/manner: 6/6/7 <br/>Aesthetics/Technical: 7/6 <br/>Presentation: 5 <br/>Total: 6.2 <br/>Vote: 6<br/> <br/>Remarks: This is an immensely and, I think, universally appealing image. The pattern and interest in the upper (background) section is well enough established to consider the composition appropriate and apt. <br/> <br/>Being somewhat familiar with photographing similar scenes under similar conditions, I can appreciate the chosen exposure for proliferating the shadows. The myriad highlights (reflected from the sand), however, make for a slightly harsh and gritty texture, especially when sharpened, which is fine at this resolution but likely challenge our appreciative ability at a much higher one. (?)</td>', 'Energy/Range/Story: 6/7/6 Composition/perspective/manner: 6/6/7 Aesthetics/Technical: 7/6 Presentation: 5 Total: 6.2 Vote: 6 Remarks: This is an immensely and, I think, universally appealing image. The pattern and interest in the upper (background) section is well enough established to consider the composition appropriate and apt.  Being somewhat familiar with photographing similar scenes under similar conditions, I can appreciate the chosen exposure for proliferating the shadows. The myriad highlights (reflected from the sand), however, make for a slightly harsh and gritty texture, especially when sharpened, which is fine at this resolution but likely challenge our appreciative ability at a much higher one. (?)', '2008-03-28 00:06:57.000000', NULL, 1),
