(4604520, 661684, 67697, '<td valign="top">Lol - that is one heck of an essay.  Ok if this scored poorly, then my photo is crap because it scored lower than yours.  <br/> <br/>Ok here''s the patterns I see, for those that fail to see them (geez):<br/> <br/>1) Two trees connected by the double line.<br/>2) All the little squares<br/>3) The white lines of the cross walk.<br/>4) The barrier sticks running along the curb. (ooh and their shadows!)<br/> <br/>This is not a pattern thingy but I just noticed this and it''s pretty cool - you have a bike, it''s shadow, and then there is a white symbol of the bike in the street.  Very coolies.<br/> <br/>Great photo with lots to look at.  Fun, very fun.</td>', 'Lol - that is one heck of an essay.  Ok if this scored poorly, then my photo is crap because it scored lower than yours.   Ok here''s the patterns I see, for those that fail to see them (geez): 1) Two trees connected by the double line.2) All the little squares3) The white lines of the cross walk.4) The barrier sticks running along the curb. (ooh and their shadows!) This is not a pattern thingy but I just noticed this and it''s pretty cool - you have a bike, it''s shadow, and then there is a white symbol of the bike in the street.  Very coolies. Great photo with lots to look at.  Fun, very fun.', '2008-04-02 01:13:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4604526, 660129, 23098, '<td valign="top">Congrats!!  Cool shot.  I like the perspective and the sharpness is great. Well deserved ribbon.<br/></td>', 'Congrats!!  Cool shot.  I like the perspective and the sharpness is great. Well deserved ribbon.', '2008-04-02 01:15:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4604539, 662119, 57570, '<td valign="top">Thankyou all for ur comments. It feels nice to see this make the top 10. On how this was done.....the setup is just one diagonal of pencils interleaved at the tip. I set the camera to  long exposure and exposed the pencil tips alone using a flashlight. I moved the setup a little in both horizontal and vertical direction and then exposed the pencil tips again. Repeat this a few times.</td>', 'Thankyou all for ur comments. It feels nice to see this make the top 10. On how this was done.....the setup is just one diagonal of pencils interleaved at the tip. I set the camera to  long exposure and exposed the pencil tips alone using a flashlight. I moved the setup a little in both horizontal and vertical direction and then exposed the pencil tips again. Repeat this a few times.', '2008-04-02 01:17:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4604541, 661684, 66193, '<td valign="top">Deb, I just love this shot! To heck with the voters who couldn''t see the pattern.  I see at least 9 patterns here!  this image just begs to have the viewer linger over and explore.  And the B&amp;W conversion is spot on!  Well done, and adding to faves.</td>', 'Deb, I just love this shot! To heck with the voters who couldn''t see the pattern.  I see at least 9 patterns here!  this image just begs to have the viewer linger over and explore.  And the B&W conversion is spot on!  Well done, and adding to faves.', '2008-04-02 01:17:13.000000', NULL, 0),
