(4605693, 662175, 67152, '<td valign="top">Steve- Really good work.  It conveys the softness of the flower and yet provides a strong symmetrical pattern at the same time</td>', 'Steve- Really good work.  It conveys the softness of the flower and yet provides a strong symmetrical pattern at the same time', '2008-04-02 07:09:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605702, 661684, 67152, '<td valign="top">So Deb...You feel like me?  I really like this image and your decision to go b/w.  I find your vision and view point refreshing and I tend to be drawn to your work.  This is another example - What is the pattern?  Do I see the same one as the photographer?  Your work challenges us a bit more and I think that is actually a very good thing, but unfortunately not very rewarding if you are trying to go for a 6+ score...<br/> <br/></td>', 'So Deb...You feel like me?  I really like this image and your decision to go b/w.  I find your vision and view point refreshing and I tend to be drawn to your work.  This is another example - What is the pattern?  Do I see the same one as the photographer?  Your work challenges us a bit more and I think that is actually a very good thing, but unfortunately not very rewarding if you are trying to go for a 6+ score... ', '2008-04-02 07:15:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605725, 660604, 33352, '<td valign="top">Good finish Sandy, I like how you used the B/W to bring out the paterns..</td>', 'Good finish Sandy, I like how you used the B/W to bring out the paterns..', '2008-04-02 07:23:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605728, 661952, 67152, '<td valign="top">I think this has some solid technicals - focus, good contrast of colors, nice lines and angles, but my impression of the shot is that there is actually a few conflicting sets of patterns that disrupt the viewer.  The tire tread is a great set of patterns and carries our eyes through the image, but the spokes of the wheel is another set of patterns and one that actually confounds us a bit.  But the main patterns that don''t seem to work for me are the shadows - especially to the right of the image. A tire without the wheel on the same background with a bit more light coming from the right to fill the background - or a placement farther away from the backround so that the shadow is diminished - may have worked a lot better.</td>', 'I think this has some solid technicals - focus, good contrast of colors, nice lines and angles, but my impression of the shot is that there is actually a few conflicting sets of patterns that disrupt the viewer.  The tire tread is a great set of patterns and carries our eyes through the image, but the spokes of the wheel is another set of patterns and one that actually confounds us a bit.  But the main patterns that don''t seem to work for me are the shadows - especially to the right of the image. A tire without the wheel on the same background with a bit more light coming from the right to fill the background - or a placement farther away from the backround so that the shadow is diminished - may have worked a lot better.', '2008-04-02 07:24:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605735, 661925, 67152, '<td valign="top">Robert - I think your score suffered from a lack of scientific understanding o the viewers part and a lack of uniform patterns in the image.  I quite like your vision here to find the fractals in the tree and feel this clearly meets the challenge well in a refreshing approach.  I side with Deb that I see a bit much blue halo and I am sure some voters voted you down on it.  If I have voted, I would have likely given this a 6</td>', 'Robert - I think your score suffered from a lack of scientific understanding o the viewers part and a lack of uniform patterns in the image.  I quite like your vision here to find the fractals in the tree and feel this clearly meets the challenge well in a refreshing approach.  I side with Deb that I see a bit much blue halo and I am sure some voters voted you down on it.  If I have voted, I would have likely given this a 6', '2008-04-02 07:27:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605745, 662137, 52549, '<td valign="top">Simple, yet effective. Congrats on 4th, Richard.</td>', 'Simple, yet effective. Congrats on 4th, Richard.', '2008-04-02 07:33:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605749, 661623, 52549, '<td valign="top">Very good. Love the colour. Congrats on top 5, Oliver.</td>', 'Very good. Love the colour. Congrats on top 5, Oliver.', '2008-04-02 07:35:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605783, 662183, 60614, '<td valign="top">Congratulations.  This was a very cool shot.</td>', 'Congratulations.  This was a very cool shot.', '2008-04-02 07:48:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605795, 662183, 90495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dr.Confuser:</b></div><hr/><i> Just my opinion, and you can feel free to throw it away, but a chiched tired theme. I long for something new. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Saying this after the fact is kind of.... useless. During the voting, I can accept.<br/> <br/>Great shot JMart. You''ve pleased the masses.</td>', 'Originally posted by Dr.Confuser: Just my opinion, and you can feel free to throw it away, but a chiched tired theme. I long for something new.   Saying this after the fact is kind of.... useless. During the voting, I can accept. Great shot JMart. You''ve pleased the masses.', '2008-04-02 07:51:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605836, 661684, 49109, '<td valign="top">Most underrated in the challenge. just look at all those patterns: four different in the pavements; the borders of the pavement;  the zebra crossing; the parasols; the steps; imagine the row of trees continued endlessly right from the image... <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=630353" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/45000-49999/49109/120/630353.gif'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/45000-49999/49109/120/630353.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/45000-49999/49109/120/630353.gif"/></a></td>', 'Most underrated in the challenge. just look at all those patterns: four different in the pavements; the borders of the pavement;  the zebra crossing; the parasols; the steps; imagine the row of trees continued endlessly right from the image... ', '2008-04-02 08:05:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605853, 660678, 49109, '<td valign="top">Way underrated shot. Just wonder why you shot it at ISO 400 f/9 and 1/1000th when you could have easily used f/11, ISO 100 and 1/160th ?</td>', 'Way underrated shot. Just wonder why you shot it at ISO 400 f/9 and 1/1000th when you could have easily used f/11, ISO 100 and 1/160th ?', '2008-04-02 08:12:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605866, 660656, 58454, '<td valign="top">Great - thanks... I am so happy to be over 6 with my very first entry - this was fun and nothing can stop me now.</td>', 'Great - thanks... I am so happy to be over 6 with my very first entry - this was fun and nothing can stop me now.', '2008-04-02 08:18:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605869, 662170, 77192, '<td valign="top">I think your shot might have had the same problems mine did - too much pattern (well we both have comments to that effect anyway - I can''t see how you can meet the challenge *too much* personally). That and the slight lack of sharpness might have hurt your voting.<br/> <br/>That said, I like the angle and it''s a good fit for the challenge.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-02 07:21:05.</i></td>', 'I think your shot might have had the same problems mine did - too much pattern (well we both have comments to that effect anyway - I can''t see how you can meet the challenge *too much* personally). That and the slight lack of sharpness might have hurt your voting. That said, I like the angle and it''s a good fit for the challenge.', '2008-04-02 08:20:20.000000', '2008-04-02 08:21:05.000000', 0),
(4605870, 660880, 67152, '<td valign="top">Simply brilliant!</td>', 'Simply brilliant!', '2008-04-02 08:21:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605871, 661684, 35322, '<td valign="top">There is so much going on in this photo, that I don''t even want to start commenting on it. I will only want to say that I colud look for hours, to all those little details and still find smth new.<br/>Keep shooting this kind of pics Deb, I really do like them. Who cares if DPC do not appreciate them as they should, they are great!</td>', 'There is so much going on in this photo, that I don''t even want to start commenting on it. I will only want to say that I colud look for hours, to all those little details and still find smth new.Keep shooting this kind of pics Deb, I really do like them. Who cares if DPC do not appreciate them as they should, they are great!', '2008-04-02 08:21:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605873, 661920, 90518, '<td valign="top">yay! well done!!! taking a day off to celebrate are we...? :P<br/>congrats vlado</td>', 'yay! well done!!! taking a day off to celebrate are we...? :Pcongrats vlado', '2008-04-02 08:22:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605881, 661917, 77192, '<td valign="top">I like the composition, I think the negative space is fine.<br/> <br/>I think you might have done a little better if you could enhance the swirl somehow - quite tricky in basic though.<br/> <br/>I love the colours in this.</td>', 'I like the composition, I think the negative space is fine. I think you might have done a little better if you could enhance the swirl somehow - quite tricky in basic though. I love the colours in this.', '2008-04-02 08:27:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605886, 662065, 30982, '<td valign="top">You got a very good score from me on this one - I quite agree with your assessment of the light and pattern play of the lights against the darks and vice versa.  And in fact, the longer I look at it, the more I like it, too.  As for the score?  I dunno - maybe too busy?  Some might not like the tilt - that''s a love or hate kinda thing with some people.  You do have some good comments as to why some people didn''t care for it as much.  I''d consider that a success in a challenge, by the way.  Glad you''re pleased with it and that it came out the way you wanted it to.  That is also a success!</td>', 'You got a very good score from me on this one - I quite agree with your assessment of the light and pattern play of the lights against the darks and vice versa.  And in fact, the longer I look at it, the more I like it, too.  As for the score?  I dunno - maybe too busy?  Some might not like the tilt - that''s a love or hate kinda thing with some people.  You do have some good comments as to why some people didn''t care for it as much.  I''d consider that a success in a challenge, by the way.  Glad you''re pleased with it and that it came out the way you wanted it to.  That is also a success!', '2008-04-02 08:30:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605901, 661636, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''ll have to admit I''m not that familiar with Clarke''s writings - read some when I was much, much younger but not a lot lately.  With your explanation, though, I can clearly see what you were trying to create, and in that vein I think you succeeded.  Based on what you wrote in the thread, I can see what you mean about the leading edge - I do think you may want to try it with just a hint of blur there, then dissolving into focus in the lower center of the shot.  And I''ll suggest it, but given your explanation don''t figure it''s your thing, but do try it in B&amp;W - maybe one of the warm gray tritones.  (Bear in mind, of course, I''m a B&amp;W kinda person.)</td>', 'I''ll have to admit I''m not that familiar with Clarke''s writings - read some when I was much, much younger but not a lot lately.  With your explanation, though, I can clearly see what you were trying to create, and in that vein I think you succeeded.  Based on what you wrote in the thread, I can see what you mean about the leading edge - I do think you may want to try it with just a hint of blur there, then dissolving into focus in the lower center of the shot.  And I''ll suggest it, but given your explanation don''t figure it''s your thing, but do try it in B&W - maybe one of the warm gray tritones.  (Bear in mind, of course, I''m a B&W kinda person.)', '2008-04-02 08:37:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605921, 661684, 11854, '<td valign="top">Patterns, patterns, everywhere! I think the voting pattern of the commenters more closely resembles what the score should be. This is a beautiful picture with much to interest the viewer. I learned at your feet, lol, I guess that''s what''s wrong with my scores. I adore your style (and your wit, to wit isn''t bad either). I think you are reaching people though, 30 votes of 7 or more and zero 1''s.</td>', 'Patterns, patterns, everywhere! I think the voting pattern of the commenters more closely resembles what the score should be. This is a beautiful picture with much to interest the viewer. I learned at your feet, lol, I guess that''s what''s wrong with my scores. I adore your style (and your wit, to wit isn''t bad either). I think you are reaching people though, 30 votes of 7 or more and zero 1''s.', '2008-04-02 08:47:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605935, 661925, 11854, '<td valign="top">Verry OOB. I also have a fasination with tree branches, lol. People always gave me odd looks when I took pictures of them and showed them around though, so I stopped taking them and trying to show them to people. Now, I just sit and watch them out my window.</td>', 'Verry OOB. I also have a fasination with tree branches, lol. People always gave me odd looks when I took pictures of them and showed them around though, so I stopped taking them and trying to show them to people. Now, I just sit and watch them out my window.', '2008-04-02 08:54:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4605939, 662137, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oh darn.  I was hoping this one would ribbon.   It was my favorite!   But another honorable mention is nice too, huh?  :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oh darn.  I was hoping this one would ribbon.   It was my favorite!   But another honorable mention is nice too, huh?  :) ', '2008-04-02 08:59:07.000000', NULL, 0),
