(4606505, 660604, 15711, '<td valign="top">Heh - great finish, Sandy.  Isn''t our capitol''s rotunda beautiful????</td>', 'Heh - great finish, Sandy.  Isn''t our capitol''s rotunda beautiful????', '2008-04-02 11:22:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606517, 660187, 24454, '<td valign="top">Wow, Roz!  This is so amazing.  I wondered how you got those drops suspended like this.   This is such a beautiful nature photo.   I can see it featured in Outdoor Photographer.  I''m disappointed in the narrow minded take on what a pattern is that must have caused people not to give this the score it deserved.  I like the score your commenters gave this!   Much more fitting!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow, Roz!  This is so amazing.  I wondered how you got those drops suspended like this.   This is such a beautiful nature photo.   I can see it featured in Outdoor Photographer.  I''m disappointed in the narrow minded take on what a pattern is that must have caused people not to give this the score it deserved.  I like the score your commenters gave this!   Much more fitting! ', '2008-04-02 11:24:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606557, 660129, 66348, '<td valign="top">Incredible, amazing, stunning, to say the least. Beautiful image, wonderfully edited. Congrats on the Ribb.</td>', 'Incredible, amazing, stunning, to say the least. Beautiful image, wonderfully edited. Congrats on the Ribb.', '2008-04-02 11:41:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606614, 661067, 6845, '<td valign="top">Welcome to the just getting the 6 score crowd. You and I got in by the skin of our teeth. Great job none the less, I really liked this image.</td>', 'Welcome to the just getting the 6 score crowd. You and I got in by the skin of our teeth. Great job none the less, I really liked this image.', '2008-04-02 12:02:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606619, 661422, 80912, '<td valign="top">To answer your last question first - Yes! lol<br/> <br/>I''m one of your 8s. I loved this, your title made me think of it as "movie poster" art. Not exactly what you intended, but I still think you should have scoredd higher. Guess it''s the bias against abstracts. Even though thtat shouldn''t be the case in a "Pattern" challenge. <br/> <br/>I did see the lines more as negative space elelmets - to me the pattern (not a recurring symetrical one, obviously) was the horizontal lines of the reflection. I kept trying to see faces (who''s the star of this movie? lol).</td>', 'To answer your last question first - Yes! lol I''m one of your 8s. I loved this, your title made me think of it as "movie poster" art. Not exactly what you intended, but I still think you should have scoredd higher. Guess it''s the bias against abstracts. Even though thtat shouldn''t be the case in a "Pattern" challenge.  I did see the lines more as negative space elelmets - to me the pattern (not a recurring symetrical one, obviously) was the horizontal lines of the reflection. I kept trying to see faces (who''s the star of this movie? lol).', '2008-04-02 12:04:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606620, 662185, 6845, '<td valign="top">Hey we can''t win them all, but great shot anyway, I still stand by my choice of b&amp;w for this image, but I don''t think it would have made the score any better. Good work and keep it coming.</td>', 'Hey we can''t win them all, but great shot anyway, I still stand by my choice of b&w for this image, but I don''t think it would have made the score any better. Good work and keep it coming.', '2008-04-02 12:04:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606622, 662200, 6845, '<td valign="top">Hey even though you couldn''t do exactly what you wanted, top 20 and that score are nothing to be ashamed of. Good job and keep it going.</td>', 'Hey even though you couldn''t do exactly what you wanted, top 20 and that score are nothing to be ashamed of. Good job and keep it going.', '2008-04-02 12:05:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606629, 662072, 6845, '<td valign="top">So close to that top ten, missed it by this much --- . Well good job on leading us into battle with the high score for the week once again, that is why you are the Cpt.</td>', 'So close to that top ten, missed it by this much --- . Well good job on leading us into battle with the high score for the week once again, that is why you are the Cpt.', '2008-04-02 12:07:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606633, 660404, 6845, '<td valign="top">Good job, 5.9 is still a very good score. Keep the good work coming.</td>', 'Good job, 5.9 is still a very good score. Keep the good work coming.', '2008-04-02 12:08:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606709, 660129, 52628, '<td valign="top">Great photo and great title.</td>', 'Great photo and great title.', '2008-04-02 12:30:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606815, 662247, 30982, '<td valign="top">I liked it during voting - had an intriguing combination of patterns.  I think to score higher, though, it needed the proverbial "more".  Maybe set it at more of a diagonal to create some energy.  I don''t know.  But do note that those who liked it REALLY liked it - look at the difference between the commenter average and your score - and that was with a reasonable number of commenters!  The more I look at it, the more I see another option should you want to play some more.  If possible, set it horizontally and shoot down between the yellow lines, with the coil as the arches overhead.  Might be kinda cool that way, like a minature highway with bridges crossing it.</td>', 'I liked it during voting - had an intriguing combination of patterns.  I think to score higher, though, it needed the proverbial "more".  Maybe set it at more of a diagonal to create some energy.  I don''t know.  But do note that those who liked it REALLY liked it - look at the difference between the commenter average and your score - and that was with a reasonable number of commenters!  The more I look at it, the more I see another option should you want to play some more.  If possible, set it horizontally and shoot down between the yellow lines, with the coil as the arches overhead.  Might be kinda cool that way, like a minature highway with bridges crossing it.', '2008-04-02 12:59:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606828, 661210, 30982, '<td valign="top">What a very cool place!  And yes, the colors are magnificent.  I think for this challenge, had you focused on the left side of the shot where the cool swirlies are, it would have done better, though 5.8 and the top 20% here is NOT sucking, by the way.  Of course, by focusing on the left, you''d lose the deep blues and purples on the right which I think lend a lovely balance to this.</td>', 'What a very cool place!  And yes, the colors are magnificent.  I think for this challenge, had you focused on the left side of the shot where the cool swirlies are, it would have done better, though 5.8 and the top 20% here is NOT sucking, by the way.  Of course, by focusing on the left, you''d lose the deep blues and purples on the right which I think lend a lovely balance to this.', '2008-04-02 13:01:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606839, 662000, 84656, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> I found the border to be too bold, while the image itself is too small. try to make the most of the 640 px height you have. The black border alone would have given enough depth. If your image lost sharpness during resizing, you probably don''t use the best resizing method; in photoshop it would be "bicubic sharper" when downsizing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Tx <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=49109" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">eyewave</a>, point taken re border, without the white border the warp effect is still quite strong thoug.  Just did a test with the different resizing method and it makes a considerable difference, thanks for that<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-02 12:12:56.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by eyewave: I found the border to be too bold, while the image itself is too small. try to make the most of the 640 px height you have. The black border alone would have given enough depth. If your image lost sharpness during resizing, you probably don''t use the best resizing method; in photoshop it would be "bicubic sharper" when downsizing.   Tx  eyewave, point taken re border, without the white border the warp effect is still quite strong thoug.  Just did a test with the different resizing method and it makes a considerable difference, thanks for that', '2008-04-02 13:04:57.000000', '2008-04-02 13:12:56.000000', 0),
(4606842, 662222, 30982, '<td valign="top">First off, I''d have never known it was a pine tree, despite the hint in your title.  To me, it was simply a rather nice quiet melody with no reason to know what it actually was.  Second, that wee bit of purple is awesome.  Third, pattern?  Yes, but way too subtle for the .7 second voter (2 seconds is just too generous I think).  I like the pattern of the shadows in particular.  An excellent use of the sexy lens.</td>', 'First off, I''d have never known it was a pine tree, despite the hint in your title.  To me, it was simply a rather nice quiet melody with no reason to know what it actually was.  Second, that wee bit of purple is awesome.  Third, pattern?  Yes, but way too subtle for the .7 second voter (2 seconds is just too generous I think).  I like the pattern of the shadows in particular.  An excellent use of the sexy lens.', '2008-04-02 13:05:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606873, 661959, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very rich color, excellent light, and to me quite obviously patterned throughout the shot.  Those that commented were rather fond of it as well.  Perhaps too "quiet" (don''t you hate that?) for DPC but well suited to the challenge and a gorgeous shot.</td>', 'Very rich color, excellent light, and to me quite obviously patterned throughout the shot.  Those that commented were rather fond of it as well.  Perhaps too "quiet" (don''t you hate that?) for DPC but well suited to the challenge and a gorgeous shot.', '2008-04-02 13:13:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606930, 660656, 55838, '<td valign="top">Congratualtions!  A score of 6 on your first entry is fantastic!  Well done on a creative shot.</td>', 'Congratualtions!  A score of 6 on your first entry is fantastic!  Well done on a creative shot.', '2008-04-02 13:26:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606988, 660096, 26001, '<td valign="top">congratulations on your personal best Lydia. I am glad this one did well and finished in top 20.</td>', 'congratulations on your personal best Lydia. I am glad this one did well and finished in top 20.', '2008-04-02 13:38:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4606995, 662177, 55838, '<td valign="top">You were ripped off!  60 votes of 4 &amp; under?!!!  Sheesh! Although I can''t say that I LOVE the fingers in the composition, without them I would not realize just how tiny he is.  You have a great focus on your subject - your colors are nice - along with a pleasant DOF - it just seems that these factors alone should have eeked you out a bit better of a score!  From one of your seventeen 7''s.</td>', 'You were ripped off!  60 votes of 4 & under?!!!  Sheesh! Although I can''t say that I LOVE the fingers in the composition, without them I would not realize just how tiny he is.  You have a great focus on your subject - your colors are nice - along with a pleasant DOF - it just seems that these factors alone should have eeked you out a bit better of a score!  From one of your seventeen 7''s.', '2008-04-02 13:38:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607025, 661684, 69557, '<td valign="top">i loved this picture. while the patterns didn''t stick out for me to begin with (though i did see them on more scrutiny), i thought the picture was fantastic. the trees, the pavement, the people walking, the black-and-white-ness of it, all fit really well. <br/> <br/>interestingly, my mom (who''s on dpc as well) considered your photo her favorite [over mine :(] :).</td>', 'i loved this picture. while the patterns didn''t stick out for me to begin with (though i did see them on more scrutiny), i thought the picture was fantastic. the trees, the pavement, the people walking, the black-and-white-ness of it, all fit really well.  interestingly, my mom (who''s on dpc as well) considered your photo her favorite [over mine :(] :).', '2008-04-02 13:43:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607103, 662200, 84410, '<td valign="top">bravo!</td>', 'bravo!', '2008-04-02 14:00:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607107, 661636, 48471, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments, they''re very educational. I understand now that this image relies too much on the background and it can''t stand strongly alone.<br/> <br/>Deb, I like black and white more than colour, that''s why I try to have the latter as less as possible. I just felt it that in this case colour would be a definit feature. I''ll take your advise and try something similar in monochrome. I''ll add some shadows as well, for Don''s sake.<br/> <br/>Thanks again...</td>', 'Thanks for the comments, they''re very educational. I understand now that this image relies too much on the background and it can''t stand strongly alone. Deb, I like black and white more than colour, that''s why I try to have the latter as less as possible. I just felt it that in this case colour would be a definit feature. I''ll take your advise and try something similar in monochrome. I''ll add some shadows as well, for Don''s sake. Thanks again...', '2008-04-02 14:00:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607129, 662208, 69325, '<td valign="top">well, you met your goal for this shot and it looks like you got some valuable advice in the comments. Many people score in the 4''s on their first try. Good job breaking 5 on your first one!</td>', 'well, you met your goal for this shot and it looks like you got some valuable advice in the comments. Many people score in the 4''s on their first try. Good job breaking 5 on your first one!', '2008-04-02 14:04:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607265, 661917, 90806, '<td valign="top">Particularly at this time of year when there is only the anticipation of things coming back to life it makes me quite happy to see this picture.  The multiple patterns are great with the obvious twist of the petals and the finer detailed veining of both the petals and the sepals and the wonderful contrast zig zag where the green sepals meet the pink of the petals.  I love how the DOF is just right to be in focus from the curve of the stem to the tip of the petals.  The more I see it the more I like it.</td>', 'Particularly at this time of year when there is only the anticipation of things coming back to life it makes me quite happy to see this picture.  The multiple patterns are great with the obvious twist of the petals and the finer detailed veining of both the petals and the sepals and the wonderful contrast zig zag where the green sepals meet the pink of the petals.  I love how the DOF is just right to be in focus from the curve of the stem to the tip of the petals.  The more I see it the more I like it.', '2008-04-02 14:30:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607311, 661210, 90806, '<td valign="top">I think that the dark area that is front and center, starting in the middle and going straight down and off to the left may have taken away from this shot some.  Perhaps if it had some more light on it to show off its pattern as well the contrast of the other patterns could have been enhanced.</td>', 'I think that the dark area that is front and center, starting in the middle and going straight down and off to the left may have taken away from this shot some.  Perhaps if it had some more light on it to show off its pattern as well the contrast of the other patterns could have been enhanced.', '2008-04-02 14:40:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607365, 661684, 83313, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get this one coming around in my voting. I would have likely given it a 5. I''ve been considering this one on and off this morning, so I could try and give you some useful input. It leads the eye, but I''m not sure what it leads it to. There are numerous small subjects in the image, none of which really stand out and grab attention, but are also in front of the pattern. Perhaps a more abstract or closer in view would have scored higher. I personally tend to like images that show texture. This is one of those images that I have a hard time commenting on as it doesn''t out stand out to me in either a positive or negative way.<br/> <br/>Edited to add: <br/>I just looked over your own notes and it appears you nailed it already yourself. I can sometimes do that on my images, knowing beforehand what the comments and low votes will be for. This challenge took me for a surprise though.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-02 14:02:32.</i></td>', 'I didn''t get this one coming around in my voting. I would have likely given it a 5. I''ve been considering this one on and off this morning, so I could try and give you some useful input. It leads the eye, but I''m not sure what it leads it to. There are numerous small subjects in the image, none of which really stand out and grab attention, but are also in front of the pattern. Perhaps a more abstract or closer in view would have scored higher. I personally tend to like images that show texture. This is one of those images that I have a hard time commenting on as it doesn''t out stand out to me in either a positive or negative way. Edited to add: I just looked over your own notes and it appears you nailed it already yourself. I can sometimes do that on my images, knowing beforehand what the comments and low votes will be for. This challenge took me for a surprise though.', '2008-04-02 14:58:12.000000', '2008-04-02 15:02:32.000000', 0),
(4607414, 662170, 83313, '<td valign="top">I don''t think it is blur, so much as a lack of the fine clarity that most look for in a scene like this. Perhaps a side effect of the post processing. I will sometimes find I lose some fine detail in my effort to make something pop. Though you did have a wide aperture and slow shutter speed. I have been finding that with my SLR I can get away with bumping up the ISO to higher levels with little to no visible noise. That may be a preferable option instead of a slow shutter speed.   The image does have a neat 3-dimensional feel to it. I like the composition.</td>', 'I don''t think it is blur, so much as a lack of the fine clarity that most look for in a scene like this. Perhaps a side effect of the post processing. I will sometimes find I lose some fine detail in my effort to make something pop. Though you did have a wide aperture and slow shutter speed. I have been finding that with my SLR I can get away with bumping up the ISO to higher levels with little to no visible noise. That may be a preferable option instead of a slow shutter speed.   The image does have a neat 3-dimensional feel to it. I like the composition.', '2008-04-02 15:12:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607431, 661917, 83313, '<td valign="top">You already got my input during voting, but I thought I would let you know I gave it a 7.</td>', 'You already got my input during voting, but I thought I would let you know I gave it a 7.', '2008-04-02 15:14:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607449, 662247, 83313, '<td valign="top">I gave it an 8. I''ll add that there was a lot of detail and bold color in this that I liked. I think what probably hurt it in voting was most took the composition to be fairly deadpan.</td>', 'I gave it an 8. I''ll add that there was a lot of detail and bold color in this that I liked. I think what probably hurt it in voting was most took the composition to be fairly deadpan.', '2008-04-02 15:19:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607461, 661210, 83313, '<td valign="top">I thought the pattern was pretty obvious, even though it was a major element of the scene and not the primary subject.  I gave it a 7, BTW.</td>', 'I thought the pattern was pretty obvious, even though it was a major element of the scene and not the primary subject.  I gave it a 7, BTW.', '2008-04-02 15:22:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607466, 660187, 68586, '<td valign="top">Great capture !</td>', 'Great capture !', '2008-04-02 15:23:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607477, 662183, 83080, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dr.Confuser:</b></div><hr/><i> Just my opinion, and you can feel free to throw it away, but a chiched tired theme. I long for something new. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>OK...  chiched &amp; tired seems a little harsh to me, but you''re entitled to your opinion.<br/> <br/>I perfectly understand from reading the forums and comments on similar shots that there are some folks here at DPC who are tired of "this kind of shot", be it this exact style or other water/milk/coffee drop shots.  I''m a newbie, so perhaps I might just be naive, but drop shots are truly amazing IMHO and the possibilities for creative twists on all of these "tired themes" seem no less than for those tired old bird, waterfall, Golden Gate Bridge, baby, building, and flower themes (all of which I have to admit to also loving).  Weve all seen the exact same subjects and techniques time and time again.  Rather than asking if its been done, Id rather ask if I can do it in my own way.  Otherwise Ill never learn anything, let alone create anything worth while.<br/> <br/>Just don''t forget, whatever you''re doing with your art, chances are you''re not the first to use ANY given technique and somebody out there is already <i>over</i> what you''re doing.  It would be a real shame if that stopped you from learning in the direction you want to go.  As for me, I''m here to learn as many techniques as I can, practice my shooting, and have some fun.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Dr.Confuser: Just my opinion, and you can feel free to throw it away, but a chiched tired theme. I long for something new.  OK...  chiched & tired seems a little harsh to me, but you''re entitled to your opinion. I perfectly understand from reading the forums and comments on similar shots that there are some folks here at DPC who are tired of "this kind of shot", be it this exact style or other water/milk/coffee drop shots.  I''m a newbie, so perhaps I might just be naive, but drop shots are truly amazing IMHO and the possibilities for creative twists on all of these "tired themes" seem no less than for those tired old bird, waterfall, Golden Gate Bridge, baby, building, and flower themes (all of which I have to admit to also loving).  Weve all seen the exact same subjects and techniques time and time again.  Rather than asking if its been done, Id rather ask if I can do it in my own way.  Otherwise Ill never learn anything, let alone create anything worth while. Just don''t forget, whatever you''re doing with your art, chances are you''re not the first to use ANY given technique and somebody out there is already over what you''re doing.  It would be a real shame if that stopped you from learning in the direction you want to go.  As for me, I''m here to learn as many techniques as I can, practice my shooting, and have some fun.', '2008-04-02 15:27:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4607557, 662239, 83080, '<td valign="top">OK, someone is smoking crack if they can''t see the patterns here (or maybe that would make them see more patterns).  This is a nice shot for this challenge and I think the commenters scored a little closer to the mark.</td>', 'OK, someone is smoking crack if they can''t see the patterns here (or maybe that would make them see more patterns).  This is a nice shot for this challenge and I think the commenters scored a little closer to the mark.', '2008-04-02 15:48:41.000000', NULL, 0),
