(4608812, 660656, 83080, '<td valign="top">This is one of my top three favorites in this challenge and I actually expected to see it a lot higher to be honest.  Congratulations and I look forward to seeing your future work.</td>', 'This is one of my top three favorites in this challenge and I actually expected to see it a lot higher to be honest.  Congratulations and I look forward to seeing your future work.', '2008-04-02 22:38:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4609201, 660880, 87867, '<td valign="top">perfect picture. it stands out more because you left the person there. it would have been a little boring without him.</td>', 'perfect picture. it stands out more because you left the person there. it would have been a little boring without him.', '2008-04-02 23:51:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4609557, 662119, 26001, '<td valign="top">absolutely genius!</td>', 'absolutely genius!', '2008-04-03 01:34:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4609762, 662000, 30982, '<td valign="top">It moves when you scroll - cool!  I think I see what you mean about it being ungrounded without the frame, though.  DPC is kinda "eh" on borders - but if you like them with a shot, use them.  Try without first (which you did) then go with your gut instinct.  You picked a good subject to shoot for the challenge - great color, good exposure, pretty good composition for this subject, too.  You may also want to try shooting this with a strong diagonal - in some ways that may counteract the optical illusion just a bit.</td>', 'It moves when you scroll - cool!  I think I see what you mean about it being ungrounded without the frame, though.  DPC is kinda "eh" on borders - but if you like them with a shot, use them.  Try without first (which you did) then go with your gut instinct.  You picked a good subject to shoot for the challenge - great color, good exposure, pretty good composition for this subject, too.  You may also want to try shooting this with a strong diagonal - in some ways that may counteract the optical illusion just a bit.', '2008-04-03 04:14:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4609769, 661936, 30982, '<td valign="top">First of all, I liked this one when voting.  Having shallow DOF in the foreground of a shot is a love it or leave it kinda thing to some people.  Perhaps it''s even an acquired taste.  I personally like foreground OOF when it serves a purpose.  This is a pretty good shot - definitely meets the challenge and I agree that the colors beyond the fence really add nicely to this.  The shallow DOF, to me, emphasizes the repetition of the pattern.  If you have the chance (and think to do so - that''s the part I always forget) try shooting things like this with different settings, different focal points.  That will give you an idea of what looks good, what works.</td>', 'First of all, I liked this one when voting.  Having shallow DOF in the foreground of a shot is a love it or leave it kinda thing to some people.  Perhaps it''s even an acquired taste.  I personally like foreground OOF when it serves a purpose.  This is a pretty good shot - definitely meets the challenge and I agree that the colors beyond the fence really add nicely to this.  The shallow DOF, to me, emphasizes the repetition of the pattern.  If you have the chance (and think to do so - that''s the part I always forget) try shooting things like this with different settings, different focal points.  That will give you an idea of what looks good, what works.', '2008-04-03 04:19:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4609774, 661756, 30982, '<td valign="top">This did very well - top 50 and almost a 6.0.  You don''t have a disproportionate amount of "low" scores at all.  Perhaps there are voters who hate building reflection shots.  There are students from classes who are viewing and voting as part of their school requirement - maybe they aren''t putting much thought into it.  In any case, seven votes of 3 or lower out of nearly 300 is not unexpected by standard distribution, and is in fact quite low.  If you look at the ends - you have seven votes of 3 and lower, and 22 votes of 8 or higher.  In other words, your voting is actually skewed a bit toward the high end.  That would be a good thing!  Also, for whatever reason, there are voters for whom a 4 is average instead of a 5.  Oh - meant to start out with this - congrats on the new personal best!  I''m sure you''ll replace it with even higher scoring shots in no time at all!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-03 03:25:41.</i></td>', 'This did very well - top 50 and almost a 6.0.  You don''t have a disproportionate amount of "low" scores at all.  Perhaps there are voters who hate building reflection shots.  There are students from classes who are viewing and voting as part of their school requirement - maybe they aren''t putting much thought into it.  In any case, seven votes of 3 or lower out of nearly 300 is not unexpected by standard distribution, and is in fact quite low.  If you look at the ends - you have seven votes of 3 and lower, and 22 votes of 8 or higher.  In other words, your voting is actually skewed a bit toward the high end.  That would be a good thing!  Also, for whatever reason, there are voters for whom a 4 is average instead of a 5.  Oh - meant to start out with this - congrats on the new personal best!  I''m sure you''ll replace it with even higher scoring shots in no time at all!', '2008-04-03 04:24:44.000000', '2008-04-03 04:25:41.000000', 0),
(4609802, 661684, 18450, '<td valign="top">Deb, this is one of those images that makes me stop to linger, to enjoy. There''s so much to see, so many stories to tell. What a wonderful talent you have. And yes, I see all the patterns too.</td>', 'Deb, this is one of those images that makes me stop to linger, to enjoy. There''s so much to see, so many stories to tell. What a wonderful talent you have. And yes, I see all the patterns too.', '2008-04-03 05:43:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4609804, 660129, 36999, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon!  Great pattern too!</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon!  Great pattern too!', '2008-04-03 05:45:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4609807, 662183, 36999, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon!  Nicely done.</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon!  Nicely done.', '2008-04-03 05:45:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610073, 661936, 90806, '<td valign="top">I like this shot and I like the foreground oof and the narrow depth of field but would have preferred it a hair wider or shifted just slightly forward.  My eye is distracted by the front of the ring that is in focus being out of focus.  I think the whole image would have felt sharper if that whole ring had been in focus.</td>', 'I like this shot and I like the foreground oof and the narrow depth of field but would have preferred it a hair wider or shifted just slightly forward.  My eye is distracted by the front of the ring that is in focus being out of focus.  I think the whole image would have felt sharper if that whole ring had been in focus.', '2008-04-03 09:01:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610114, 661201, 90502, '<td valign="top">This is a photograph of a mesh pencil holder.  The bolder lines are close to the camera and the fuzzy  ones are shadows of the mesh cast from the other side of the cylindrical holder.  <br/> <br/>What I like about the photo is the appearance of depth depending how you view it.</td>', 'This is a photograph of a mesh pencil holder.  The bolder lines are close to the camera and the fuzzy  ones are shadows of the mesh cast from the other side of the cylindrical holder.   What I like about the photo is the appearance of depth depending how you view it.', '2008-04-03 09:33:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610439, 661745, 91944, '<td valign="top">How did you capture that?</td>', 'How did you capture that?', '2008-04-03 11:01:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610669, 661756, 80458, '<td valign="top">I voted this one a 4 and I wish I had done it a little higher, maybe a 6. I tend to vote lower on "less creative" shots. The thing I dont like is the dark silhouetted building on the right. I think it detracts from your image a bit. One of the things I really like, which you probably noticed too, is the curviture of the building. <br/> <br/>Cliche as it seems- what really matters, despite the low scores you received, is that you like it</td>', 'I voted this one a 4 and I wish I had done it a little higher, maybe a 6. I tend to vote lower on "less creative" shots. The thing I dont like is the dark silhouetted building on the right. I think it detracts from your image a bit. One of the things I really like, which you probably noticed too, is the curviture of the building.  Cliche as it seems- what really matters, despite the low scores you received, is that you like it', '2008-04-03 11:55:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610705, 660129, 67343, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your first ribbon. Great framing and design. :)</td>', 'Congratulations on your first ribbon. Great framing and design. :)', '2008-04-03 12:07:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610837, 661684, 87808, '<td valign="top">If I remember correctly I think I gave this a 7.  I am not sure why you got so many low votes on this one.  There are patterns everywhere on this. <br/> <br/>I foun d it to be sharp, clean, in focus, good use of colour. Being BW took away some of the busyness of the photo.  There where alot of people in the photo which didnt help, but trying to get them to go away would have been impossible!!! Well unless you started tossing water ballons!.<br/> <br/>No I think you hit the challenge on the head with this one, many patterns from square to wiggly to clean lines.</td>', 'If I remember correctly I think I gave this a 7.  I am not sure why you got so many low votes on this one.  There are patterns everywhere on this.  I foun d it to be sharp, clean, in focus, good use of colour. Being BW took away some of the busyness of the photo.  There where alot of people in the photo which didnt help, but trying to get them to go away would have been impossible!!! Well unless you started tossing water ballons!. No I think you hit the challenge on the head with this one, many patterns from square to wiggly to clean lines.', '2008-04-03 12:55:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610853, 661952, 87808, '<td valign="top">Havent read any one else comments yet, so here is what I see. <br/> <br/>Love the yellow against the black.  The yellow bit on the tire ties it into the background too.  I like the angle on this, it is coming forward and is right in your face.  <br/> <br/>The thing that I keep looking at though is the white thing on the tire, is it a cobweb?  it keep drawing my eye to it to see what it is and the tiny leaf stuck in your ridge.  Isnt it silly as to what we find when we study the pictures. <br/> <br/>I personally would have liked to have seen the right side of the tire tread a bit more though rather than blackness and no detail. <br/> <br/>I scored this one a 7.</td>', 'Havent read any one else comments yet, so here is what I see.  Love the yellow against the black.  The yellow bit on the tire ties it into the background too.  I like the angle on this, it is coming forward and is right in your face.   The thing that I keep looking at though is the white thing on the tire, is it a cobweb?  it keep drawing my eye to it to see what it is and the tiny leaf stuck in your ridge.  Isnt it silly as to what we find when we study the pictures.  I personally would have liked to have seen the right side of the tire tread a bit more though rather than blackness and no detail.  I scored this one a 7.', '2008-04-03 13:00:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610983, 661745, 35357, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Aleema:</b></div><hr/><i> How did you capture that? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I took a few dozen shots, trying to get a decent composition.  My eye was quite sore by the end, due to the midday sun.  I held the camera a little bit away from my face to lessen the brightness of the sun through the viewfinder. :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by Aleema: How did you capture that?  I took a few dozen shots, trying to get a decent composition.  My eye was quite sore by the end, due to the midday sun.  I held the camera a little bit away from my face to lessen the brightness of the sun through the viewfinder. :-)', '2008-04-03 14:10:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610986, 662170, 87808, '<td valign="top">this is what I see when i look at it. <br/> <br/>it is an amzing picture to say the least.  But I think it really needs to be pin sharp, it does seem oof.  The other thing that i noticed is and I know there isnt, but it looks like burning on the gold.  sort of a blackish shadow on there, it appears on the lower left of the shot to within the white. <br/> <br/>magnificent colours here, amazing patterns, you are so lucky to be able to be there and see this. <br/> <br/></td>', 'this is what I see when i look at it.  it is an amzing picture to say the least.  But I think it really needs to be pin sharp, it does seem oof.  The other thing that i noticed is and I know there isnt, but it looks like burning on the gold.  sort of a blackish shadow on there, it appears on the lower left of the shot to within the white.  magnificent colours here, amazing patterns, you are so lucky to be able to be there and see this.  ', '2008-04-03 14:13:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4610991, 661917, 87808, '<td valign="top">i gave this an 8.  I liked to softness of teh curving pattern that you got in hsi fower ,whilst still keeping the background darker.<br/> <br/>You have kept the details as sharp as possible in this, I am wondering if the angle could be a little differnt.  The only reason I am saying this is the brown stalk is very much there, I am not sure if it is takign away from teh picture or not. <br/> <br/>I am a lover of negative space, but also wondering if it was taken in just a tad bit on the left side, not much just a tad. <br/> <br/>Overall, the pattern is soft and flowing the leading line of hte flower is great.</td>', 'i gave this an 8.  I liked to softness of teh curving pattern that you got in hsi fower ,whilst still keeping the background darker. You have kept the details as sharp as possible in this, I am wondering if the angle could be a little differnt.  The only reason I am saying this is the brown stalk is very much there, I am not sure if it is takign away from teh picture or not.  I am a lover of negative space, but also wondering if it was taken in just a tad bit on the left side, not much just a tad.  Overall, the pattern is soft and flowing the leading line of hte flower is great.', '2008-04-03 14:19:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4611163, 662089, 30982, '<td valign="top">It was definitely a pattern to me and those who commented obviously thought so.  I think Ivo hit it in the thread, though - geometric patterns were the order of the day, and those patterns had to be very well organized and very clean and uncluttered.</td>', 'It was definitely a pattern to me and those who commented obviously thought so.  I think Ivo hit it in the thread, though - geometric patterns were the order of the day, and those patterns had to be very well organized and very clean and uncluttered.', '2008-04-03 15:35:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4611317, 662066, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is a good entry for the challenge, I think.  You have a good strong diagonal composition, and a subject that makes the viewer pause for a minute to figure it out.  Good choice of aperture to get a deep depth of field.  And yes the focus is very good.  As for why it didn''t score higher?  Hmmm... the only thing I can think of is the "midday" part - I wonder if a shot later in the day with the sun at a lower angle would be a bit less harsh on the gold and allow more of the texture and structure of the roses to show through.</td>', 'This is a good entry for the challenge, I think.  You have a good strong diagonal composition, and a subject that makes the viewer pause for a minute to figure it out.  Good choice of aperture to get a deep depth of field.  And yes the focus is very good.  As for why it didn''t score higher?  Hmmm... the only thing I can think of is the "midday" part - I wonder if a shot later in the day with the sun at a lower angle would be a bit less harsh on the gold and allow more of the texture and structure of the roses to show through.', '2008-04-03 16:22:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4611340, 661094, 22390, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for the comments. The buildings are in fact facing Paris and the Eiffel Tower. It was impossible include it in the picture.</td>', 'Thanks to all for the comments. The buildings are in fact facing Paris and the Eiffel Tower. It was impossible include it in the picture.', '2008-04-03 16:30:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4611445, 662089, 67697, '<td valign="top">I didn''t see anything wrong with it.  I liked it.  Have you tried this in black and white?  I''m not thinking about the patterns challenge when I say this but I am thinking that this would be quite striking in B&amp;W.</td>', 'I didn''t see anything wrong with it.  I liked it.  Have you tried this in black and white?  I''m not thinking about the patterns challenge when I say this but I am thinking that this would be quite striking in B&W.', '2008-04-03 17:00:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4611768, 661713, 23484, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot. The trees are just like people reaching their arms out. This would be a good shot for a personification challenge.  At least in my opinion.</td>', 'Beautiful shot. The trees are just like people reaching their arms out. This would be a good shot for a personification challenge.  At least in my opinion.', '2008-04-03 19:25:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4611887, 661231, 23484, '<td valign="top">WOW, that''s all I can think of to say!</td>', 'WOW, that''s all I can think of to say!', '2008-04-03 20:09:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4611925, 661684, 6999, '<td valign="top">Reminds me of Kertesz''s great shot from the lower tier of the Eiffel Tower. Excellent work.</td>', 'Reminds me of Kertesz''s great shot from the lower tier of the Eiffel Tower. Excellent work.', '2008-04-03 20:40:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4611977, 661422, 76217, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Donna21:</b></div><hr/><i> To answer your last question first - Yes! lol<br/> <br/>I''m one of your 8s. I loved this, your title made me think of it as "movie poster" art. Not exactly what you intended, but I still think you should have scoredd higher. Guess it''s the bias against abstracts. Even though thtat shouldn''t be the case in a "Pattern" challenge. <br/> <br/>I did see the lines more as negative space elelmets - to me the pattern (not a recurring symetrical one, obviously) was the horizontal lines of the reflection. I kept trying to see faces (who''s the star of this movie? lol). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for answering the question. There are several stars depending on your perspective. The first is George Washington at the upper left and the last is ET the extraterrestrial on the lower right. James Bond and Michael Jordan are interspersed as well.<br/> <br/>Now, really drilling deep into the abyss, does anyone check back to see if, after they make a comment, the person who took the photograph responds in kind? Particularly if its several days later?<br/> <br/>;)</td>', 'Originally posted by Donna21: To answer your last question first - Yes! lol I''m one of your 8s. I loved this, your title made me think of it as "movie poster" art. Not exactly what you intended, but I still think you should have scoredd higher. Guess it''s the bias against abstracts. Even though thtat shouldn''t be the case in a "Pattern" challenge.  I did see the lines more as negative space elelmets - to me the pattern (not a recurring symetrical one, obviously) was the horizontal lines of the reflection. I kept trying to see faces (who''s the star of this movie? lol).   Thank you for answering the question. There are several stars depending on your perspective. The first is George Washington at the upper left and the last is ET the extraterrestrial on the lower right. James Bond and Michael Jordan are interspersed as well. Now, really drilling deep into the abyss, does anyone check back to see if, after they make a comment, the person who took the photograph responds in kind? Particularly if its several days later? ;)', '2008-04-03 21:12:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612016, 661745, 91944, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the response. Once again great picture.</td>', 'Thanks for the response. Once again great picture.', '2008-04-03 21:38:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612017, 662137, 27133, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.</td>', 'Beautiful.', '2008-04-03 21:39:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612076, 660129, 76335, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> Lunchtime in the city again, huh? very good shot, I like the slight red cast </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wow, Oliver, you were on to me as soon as the starting gates flew open on this one. This means that either I''m developing a highly original style (which would be good) or that I''m becoming hopelessly predictable (not so good). I have to admit I''m running out of buildings to shoot; that hour for lunch (give or take) implies a certain radius. Anyway, thanks for your comments and support!</td>', 'Originally posted by eyewave: Lunchtime in the city again, huh? very good shot, I like the slight red cast   Wow, Oliver, you were on to me as soon as the starting gates flew open on this one. This means that either I''m developing a highly original style (which would be good) or that I''m becoming hopelessly predictable (not so good). I have to admit I''m running out of buildings to shoot; that hour for lunch (give or take) implies a certain radius. Anyway, thanks for your comments and support!', '2008-04-03 22:18:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612100, 661623, 76335, '<td valign="top">This is terrific. The colors and symmetery are appealing, and the POV is pure genius. Very abstract -- my kind of shot.</td>', 'This is terrific. The colors and symmetery are appealing, and the POV is pure genius. Very abstract -- my kind of shot.', '2008-04-03 22:24:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612133, 662183, 76335, '<td valign="top">Yes this is cliche, and yes it''s been done to death, but most likely for a good reason -- people love this kind of stuff! (The proof is in the ribbon.) Dr. Confuser''s opinion is valid, but it doesn''t say much about your particular shot. I don''t mind a cliche so long as a.) the artist brings something original to it, and b.) it''s well executed. You''ve succeeded on both counts. Nice work! Keep doing what you''re doing, and congrats on your first ribbon.</td>', 'Yes this is cliche, and yes it''s been done to death, but most likely for a good reason -- people love this kind of stuff! (The proof is in the ribbon.) Dr. Confuser''s opinion is valid, but it doesn''t say much about your particular shot. I don''t mind a cliche so long as a.) the artist brings something original to it, and b.) it''s well executed. You''ve succeeded on both counts. Nice work! Keep doing what you''re doing, and congrats on your first ribbon.', '2008-04-03 22:32:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612142, 662066, 83080, '<td valign="top">I really liked this one and I ended up giving it a 6.  My favorite part about it is the composition along with an interesting subject.  On the down side, the sky has some posterization and it feels a little flat to me.  I wonder if this would pop a little better with the saturation pushed up along with a slight lightness increase and a light to medium contrast curve.  I think the average quick-click (or key-stroke) voter may be more negatively impacted by too little than too much in areas like that.  <br/> <br/>Of course, this is all just my humble opinion.  You really did take a nice photo here.</td>', 'I really liked this one and I ended up giving it a 6.  My favorite part about it is the composition along with an interesting subject.  On the down side, the sky has some posterization and it feels a little flat to me.  I wonder if this would pop a little better with the saturation pushed up along with a slight lightness increase and a light to medium contrast curve.  I think the average quick-click (or key-stroke) voter may be more negatively impacted by too little than too much in areas like that.   Of course, this is all just my humble opinion.  You really did take a nice photo here.', '2008-04-03 22:35:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612650, 660681, 37424, '<td valign="top">Congrats. Excellent image!</td>', 'Congrats. Excellent image!', '2008-04-04 03:22:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612719, 661756, 49109, '<td valign="top">I voted this a 6, it''s a good photo but nothing spectacular. Would have given a 7 if there wasn''t the slight distortion visible at the left edge and the bold black border that seems to make the image darker than it is.<br/> <br/>Besides that, have a lok at the ascores given to most ribbon winners (especially those with strong colors), they all get 1s, 2s and 3s. There''s nothing you can do to stop those people.</td>', 'I voted this a 6, it''s a good photo but nothing spectacular. Would have given a 7 if there wasn''t the slight distortion visible at the left edge and the bold black border that seems to make the image darker than it is. Besides that, have a lok at the ascores given to most ribbon winners (especially those with strong colors), they all get 1s, 2s and 3s. There''s nothing you can do to stop those people.', '2008-04-04 04:02:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4612985, 660604, 57886, '<td valign="top">Great picture AS always Sandy - your average is GREAT.... this will be my mission, average over 6 ;o) Thanks for all the kind words toward my pictures you are always soooo nice - THANKS.<br/> <br/>Did you have a look on Ipernity?<br/> <br/>Love, Ragga.</td>', 'Great picture AS always Sandy - your average is GREAT.... this will be my mission, average over 6 ;o) Thanks for all the kind words toward my pictures you are always soooo nice - THANKS. Did you have a look on Ipernity? Love, Ragga.', '2008-04-04 08:04:28.000000', NULL, 0),
