(4613920, 662203, 62318, '<td valign="top">I''m a big fan of cool tones. Nice pattern and the dirt/specs break it up just enough to keep the composition engaging.</td>', 'I''m a big fan of cool tones. Nice pattern and the dirt/specs break it up just enough to keep the composition engaging.', '2008-04-04 13:44:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4613931, 661684, 62318, '<td valign="top">Putting in your own favorite photo, good stuff Deb. Love the perspective. <br/> <br/>For some reason this feels like London, by the Tower of London. Where is this? Curious. <br/> <br/>Funny dissertation by the way... lol</td>', 'Putting in your own favorite photo, good stuff Deb. Love the perspective.  For some reason this feels like London, by the Tower of London. Where is this? Curious.  Funny dissertation by the way... lol', '2008-04-04 13:47:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4613934, 662089, 62318, '<td valign="top">Very cool pattern. Really enjoy the mix of chaotic branches and orderly bricks.</td>', 'Very cool pattern. Really enjoy the mix of chaotic branches and orderly bricks.', '2008-04-04 13:48:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4613938, 661885, 62318, '<td valign="top">I like the warm tones and a nice take on the challenge.</td>', 'I like the warm tones and a nice take on the challenge.', '2008-04-04 13:49:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4613940, 662150, 62318, '<td valign="top">Beautiful comp, light and focus.</td>', 'Beautiful comp, light and focus.', '2008-04-04 13:50:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4615148, 660187, 68035, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a super image and thank you not onlt for it but for the description of how the water was suspended (which now I know seems obvious, but didnt before hand)<br/> <br/>I love the dof you used which creates a seamless move from pinpoint sharpness to gentle blur<br/> <br/>Cool idea fantastically executed</td>', 'Wow, what a super image and thank you not onlt for it but for the description of how the water was suspended (which now I know seems obvious, but didnt before hand) I love the dof you used which creates a seamless move from pinpoint sharpness to gentle blur Cool idea fantastically executed', '2008-04-05 03:38:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4615166, 661959, 68035, '<td valign="top">Slightly unusually take on the challenge which actually works very nicely.  Love the colouring that you have achieved which really does give the shot the aquatic feel of the title<br/> <br/>Very nice</td>', 'Slightly unusually take on the challenge which actually works very nicely.  Love the colouring that you have achieved which really does give the shot the aquatic feel of the title Very nice', '2008-04-05 03:54:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4615172, 662150, 68035, '<td valign="top">I love the delicacy of this shot, the sharpness of the middle fold of lace is stunning and fantastically accentuated by the fore and back ground bokeh<br/> <br/>Very nice B&amp;W conversion as well, stong without being overpowering<br/> <br/>Looks like at least one of us is getting to grips with their macro lens<br/> <br/>Excellent<br/> <br/></td>', 'I love the delicacy of this shot, the sharpness of the middle fold of lace is stunning and fantastically accentuated by the fore and back ground bokeh Very nice B&W conversion as well, stong without being overpowering Looks like at least one of us is getting to grips with their macro lens Excellent ', '2008-04-05 03:58:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4615183, 660604, 68035, '<td valign="top">Sometimes your pictures almost make me cry.<br/> <br/>Not only because of their wonderful intinsic beauty but also because I realise my own inadequacies<br/> <br/>I have tried to take an image like this of a building in the UK loads of times and have never produced anything that comes even within touching distance of this<br/> <br/>Wonderful dof gives sharpness throughout, the lighting gives the image a luminosity which is breathtaking and the pattern itself is just incredible<br/> <br/>In our offices we have a number of large framed B&amp;W shots of abstract architectural patterns and let me tell you that none of them are as good as this<br/> <br/>Another one of your images that is heading straight to my favourites</td>', 'Sometimes your pictures almost make me cry. Not only because of their wonderful intinsic beauty but also because I realise my own inadequacies I have tried to take an image like this of a building in the UK loads of times and have never produced anything that comes even within touching distance of this Wonderful dof gives sharpness throughout, the lighting gives the image a luminosity which is breathtaking and the pattern itself is just incredible In our offices we have a number of large framed B&W shots of abstract architectural patterns and let me tell you that none of them are as good as this Another one of your images that is heading straight to my favourites', '2008-04-05 04:10:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4615320, 660187, 48228, '<td valign="top">Awesome image from you Roz, and again you were robbed, as this deserved a higher score IMO.....</td>', 'Awesome image from you Roz, and again you were robbed, as this deserved a higher score IMO.....', '2008-04-05 08:34:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4616233, 662183, 14476, '<td valign="top">Very, very well done.  And thanks for posting the steps.</td>', 'Very, very well done.  And thanks for posting the steps.', '2008-04-05 13:00:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4616391, 660129, 73250, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot...the angle and depth really work! Congrats on a well deserved win!</td>', 'Beautiful shot...the angle and depth really work! Congrats on a well deserved win!', '2008-04-05 14:19:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4617413, 662222, 90658, '<td valign="top">So they were pine needles?<br/> <br/>I really thought they were river reeds.  Here in the Pacific Northwest, especially in the high desert areas, they are plentiful.  So my mind went with something known and I made the wrong assumption.  Interestingly enough, the "whistling reeds" have purple flowers.  So that would be why I thought you "erased" the pattern of the stalks...didn''t know they were pine needles.<br/> <br/>BTW - I did give it a pretty high score within this challenge.</td>', 'So they were pine needles? I really thought they were river reeds.  Here in the Pacific Northwest, especially in the high desert areas, they are plentiful.  So my mind went with something known and I made the wrong assumption.  Interestingly enough, the "whistling reeds" have purple flowers.  So that would be why I thought you "erased" the pattern of the stalks...didn''t know they were pine needles. BTW - I did give it a pretty high score within this challenge.', '2008-04-06 00:37:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4617432, 660634, 69668, '<td valign="top">So glad to see this ribbon.  A favorite of mine from the challenge.</td>', 'So glad to see this ribbon.  A favorite of mine from the challenge.', '2008-04-06 00:47:57.000000', NULL, 0),
